{0 ical}

iCalendar for OCaml. An implementation of
{{:https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545.html}RFC 5545} with the properties of
{{:https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7986.html}RFC 7986}.

{1 The entry point}

{!Ical} is the single module of the library. An {!Ical.t} is a [VCALENDAR]
component, and a {!Ical.Component.t} is a name, a list of
{!Ical.Property.t} and the components nested in it.

- {!Ical.Property} reads a value as the data type the caller asks for, and
  {!Ical.Value_type} names those types.
- {!Ical.Date}, {!Ical.Duration} and {!Ical.Recur} hold the date, time,
  duration, period and recurrence rule value types.
- {!Ical.Registry} lists the registered properties with their default value
  types and the properties each component requires and allows.

{1 Lossless by design}

The reader keeps every property and component, known or unknown, with its
parameters and wire value, and the writer puts them back. The content line
syntax of {{:https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545.html#section-3.1} RFC 5545
Section 3.1} is that of {{:https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6350.html} RFC
6350}, so the reader comes from the [vcard] library.

{1 What is not here}

Recurrence rules are read and written but not expanded. A CalDAV server expands
them on request, and a client that needs instances asks it to,
{{:https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4791.html#section-9.6.5} RFC 4791 Section
9.6.5}.
